ViewPropertyAnimator: AOSP lifecycle (one per view, auto-start, property hand-off, cancel)

View.animate() returns one cached animator, so view.animate().cancel() reaches an animation started earlier. Property calls read the start value at call time and post the starter on the view, so an animation starts on the next frame without start(). A property taken by a new animation is removed from the running one (cancelled when left empty). withStartAction/withEndAction belong to one animation; the end action is skipped and values stay put on cancel. MACAPK_TRACE_VPA=1 logs start/cancel. Measured victim: Instagram's editor fades its action bar back in with animate().withEndAction(..).alpha(1f) and no start(); after the music sheet closed the bar and its back arrow stayed at alpha 0.

